    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Moreover, Papias himself, in the introduction to his books, makes it manifest that he was not himself a hearer and eye-witness of the holy apostles;",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "but he tells us that he received the truths of our religion from those who were acquainted with them [the apostles] in the following words:]",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But I shall not be unwilling to put down, along with my interpretations, whatsoever instructions I received with care at any time from the elders, and stored up with care in my memory, assuring you at the same time of their truth.",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For I did not, like the multitude, take pleasure in those who spoke much, but in those who taught the truth;",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "nor in those who related strange commandments, but in those who rehearsed the commandments given by the Lord to faith, and proceeding from truth itself.",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "If, then, any one who had attended on the elders came, I asked minutely after their sayings,—what Andrew or Peter said, or what was said by Philip, or by Thomas,",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "or by James, or by John, or by Matthew, or by any other of the Lord’s disciples: which things Aristion and the presbyter John, the disciples of the Lord, say.",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.i.1.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.i.1.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For I imagined that what was to be got from books was not so profitable to me as what came from the living and abiding voice.",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.ii",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.ii",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "[The early Christians] called those who practised a godly guilelessness, children, [as is stated by Papias in the first book of the Lord’s Expositions, and by Clemens Alexandrinus in his Pædagogue.]",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iii",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iii",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Judas walked about in this world a sad example of impiety; for his body having swollen to such an extent that he could not pass where a chariot could pass easily, he was crushed by the chariot, so that his bowels gushed out.",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iv.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iv.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "As the elders who saw John the disciple of the Lord remembered that they had heard from him how the Lord taught in regard to those times, and said]:",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iv.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iv.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "“The days will come in which vines shall grow, having each ten thousand branches, and in each branch ten thousand twigs, and in each true twig ten thousand shoots,",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iv.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iv.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and in every one of the shoots ten thousand clusters, and on every one of the clusters ten thousand grapes, and every grape when pressed will give five-and-twenty metretes of wine.",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iv.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iv.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And when any one of the saints shall lay hold of a cluster, another shall cry out, ‘I am a better cluster, take me;",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.iv.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.iv.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "bless the Lord through me.’ In like manner, [He said] that a grain of wheat would produce ten thousand ears, and that every ear would have ten thousand grains,",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
