  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "[Papias, who is now mentioned by us, affirms that he received the sayings of the apostles from those who accompanied them, and he moreover asserts that he heard in person Aristion and the presbyter John.",
    "chunk_index": 36,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Accordingly he mentions them frequently by name, and in his writings gives their traditions. Our notice of these circumstances may not be without its use.",
    "chunk_index": 37,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "It may also be worth while to add to the statements of Papias already given, other passages of his in which he relates some miraculous deeds, stating that he acquired the knowledge of them from tradition.",
    "chunk_index": 38,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The residence of the Apostle Philip with his daughters in Hierapolis has been mentioned above.",
    "chunk_index": 39,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s5",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s5",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "We must now point out how Papias, who lived at the same time, relates that he had received a wonderful narrative from the daughters of Philip. For he relates that a dead man was raised to life in his day.",
    "chunk_index": 40,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s6",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s6",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He also mentions another miracle relating to Justus, surnamed Barsabas, how he swallowed a deadly poison, and received no harm, on account of the grace of the Lord.",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s7",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s7",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "The same person, moreover, has set down other things as coming to him from unwritten tradition, amongst these some strange parables and instructions of the Saviour, and some other things of a more fabulous nature.",
    "chunk_index": 42,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s8",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s8",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Amongst these he says that there will be a millennium after the resurrection from the dead, when the personal reign of Christ will be established on this earth.",
    "chunk_index": 43,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s9",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s9",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "He moreover hands down, in his own writing, other narratives given by the previously mentioned Aristion of the Lord’s sayings, and the traditions of the presbyter John.",
    "chunk_index": 44,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s10",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s10",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "For information on these points, we can merely refer our readers to the books themselves; but now, to the extracts already made, we shall add, as being a matter of primary importance,",
    "chunk_index": 45,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s11",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s11",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "a tradition regarding Mark who wrote the Gospel, which he [Papias] has given in the following words]: And the presbyter said this. Mark having become the interpreter of Peter, wrote down accurately whatsoever he remembered.",
    "chunk_index": 46,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s12",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s12",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "It was not, however, in exact order that he related the sayings or deeds of Christ. For he neither heard the Lord nor accompanied Him.",
    "chunk_index": 47,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s13",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s13",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "But afterwards, as I said, he accompanied Peter, who accommodated his instructions to the necessities [of his hearers], but with no intention of giving a regular narrative of the Lord’s sayings.",
    "chunk_index": 48,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s14",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s14",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Wherefore Mark made no mistake in thus writing some things as he remembered them. For of one thing he took especial care, not to omit anything he had heard, and not to put anything fictitious into the statements.",
    "chunk_index": 49,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s15",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s15",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "[This is what is related by Papias regarding Mark; but with regard to Matthew he has made the following statements]:",
    "chunk_index": 50,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s16",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s16",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Matthew put together the oracles [of the Lord] in the Hebrew language, and each one interpreted them as best he could.",
    "chunk_index": 51,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s17",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s17",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "[The same person uses proofs from the First Epistle of John, and from the Epistle of Peter in like manner.",
    "chunk_index": 52,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vi.s18",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vi.s18",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And he also gives another story of a woman who was accused of many sins before the Lord, which is to be found in the Gospel according to the Hebrews.]",
    "chunk_index": 53,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vii.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vii.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Papias thus speaks, word for word: To some of them [angels] He gave dominion over the arrangement of the world, and He commissioned them to exercise their dominion well.",
    "chunk_index": 54,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.vii.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.vii.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "And he says, immediately after this: but it happened that their arrangement came to nothing.",
    "chunk_index": 55,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.viii.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.viii.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "With regard to the inspiration of the book (Revelation), we deem it superfluous to add another word;",
    "chunk_index": 56,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.viii.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.viii.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "for the blessed Gregory Theologus and Cyril, and even men of still older date, Papias, Irenæus, Methodius, and Hippolytus, bore entirely satisfactory testimony to it.",
    "chunk_index": 57,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.ix.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.ix.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Taking occasion from Papias of Hierapolis, the illustrious, a disciple of the apostle who leaned on the bosom of Christ, and Clemens, and Pantænus the priest of [the Church] of the Alexandrians,",
    "chunk_index": 58,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.ix.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.ix.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "and the wise Ammonius, the ancient and first expositors, who agreed with each other, who understood the work of the six days as referring to Christ and the whole Church.",
    "chunk_index": 59,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.x.s1",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.x.s1",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "(1.) Mary the mother of the Lord; (2.) Mary the wife of Cleophas or Alphæus, who was the mother of James the bishop and apostle, and of Simon and Thaddeus, and of one Joseph;",
    "chunk_index": 60,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.x.s2",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.x.s2",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "(3.) Mary Salome, wife of Zebedee, mother of John the evangelist and James; (4.) Mary Magdalene. These four are found in the Gospel.",
    "chunk_index": 61,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.x.s3",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.x.s3",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "James and Judas and Joseph were sons of an aunt (2) of the Lord’s. James also and John were sons of another aunt (3) of the Lord’s.",
    "chunk_index": 62,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
      100,
      130
    ],
    "date_confidence": "approximate",
    "out_of_period": false,
    "translation_group_id": null
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments#Papias.x.s4",
    "work_id": "anf-works/papias-fragments",
    "canonical_ref": "Papias.x.s4",
    "language": "eng",
    "text": "Mary (2), mother of James the Less and Joseph, wife of Alphæus was the sister of Mary the mother of the Lord, whom John names of Cleophas, either from her father or from the family of the clan, or for some other reason.",
    "chunk_index": 63,
    "context_before": null,
    "context_after": null,
    "date_composed": 120,
    "date_range": [
